# Contact and Verification

## 1. Purpose

This document establishes a single, authoritative point of contact for all matters relating to Vipto, and explains how any Vipto-related claim, record, or credential can be verified. It exists to ensure that interns, contributors, employers, educational institutions, and members of the public have one reliable channel through which to reach Vipto, rather than relying on informal or unofficial sources.

## 2. Official Contact Channel

**Email:** vipto.app@gmail.com
**Owner:** Ayush Vaidya

This is Vipto's sole official contact address for all organizational, legal, internship, certificate, and general inquiries. Communications purporting to be from Vipto through any other channel should not be treated as authoritative without independent confirmation through this address.

## 3. Official GitHub Organization

**GitHub Organization:** https://github.com/Vipto

Vipto's official source code, engineering activity, and version-controlled development history are maintained exclusively under this GitHub Organization. Repositories, forks, or profiles claiming affiliation with Vipto outside of this organization are not officially recognized unless separately confirmed.

## 4. Official LinkedIn Presence

Vipto maintains an official LinkedIn presence for public updates, announcements, and professional visibility. Any LinkedIn profile or page claiming to represent Vipto should be verified against Vipto's officially linked presence before being relied upon.

## 5. Product and Application Links

Where applicable, official links to Vipto's published application (including any Google Play Store listing) are made available through Vipto's official GitHub Organization profile and LinkedIn presence. These listings should be treated as authoritative in preference to any third-party mirror or unofficial listing.

## 6. Internship-Related Contact

All inquiries relating to Vipto's internship program — including applications, ongoing internship matters, and questions regarding internship terms — should be directed to vipto.app@gmail.com. This is also the correct channel for interns to raise concerns regarding their internship engagement.

## 7. Certificate Verification Contact

Any request to verify an internship certificate, confirmation letter, or experience document issued by Vipto should be sent to vipto.app@gmail.com. Requests should include the intern's full name, the stated internship period, and, where available, any reference number appearing on the document being verified.

## 8. Legal and Organizational Queries

Questions concerning Vipto's legal or organizational status, as described in [`legal.md`](./legal.md), should be directed to the same official contact address. Vipto will respond to good-faith inquiries regarding its organizational status to the extent it is able to do so factually.

## 9. Security Reporting

Security concerns or suspected vulnerabilities relating to Vipto's systems or repositories should be reported in accordance with the process set out in [`security.md`](./security.md), using the same official contact channel. Security reports should not be disclosed publicly prior to acknowledgment and resolution.

## 10. General Inquiries

General inquiries regarding Vipto — including product inquiries, partnership interest, or media inquiries — may also be directed to vipto.app@gmail.com. Vipto will make reasonable efforts to respond to legitimate inquiries in a timely manner.

## 11. Information Required for Verification Requests

To enable an efficient and accurate response, any verification request should include: the full name of the individual whose association with Vipto is being verified; the nature of the claim being verified (for example, internship period, role, or certificate authenticity); any reference number, document, or screenshot supporting the request; and the requester's own name, affiliation, and contact details, where the requester is a third party such as an employer or institution.

## 12. Authorized Confirmation

Only Vipto's authorized representatives, responding through the official contact channel set out in this document, are entitled to confirm or deny the authenticity of any Vipto-related record, internship, or certificate. Confirmations obtained through any other means — including informal messages, social media, or unofficial forwarding of documents — should not be relied upon as authoritative.
